GlesRenderer::context_id() unwraps the ContextId stored in the EGL context
user data by GlesRenderer::with_capabilities(). When that entry is missing,
the panic fires inside an extern "C" Wayland dispatch callback, which cannot
unwind, so the compositor aborts with SIGABRT instead of failing gracefully.

Happened 3 times with niri 26.04 + smithay ff5fa7df (2026-11-07/08), from
GpuManager::early_import_buffer -> import_on_src_node -> context_id. The
source inserts the ContextId unconditionally with insert_if_missing_threadsafe,
so a missing entry should be impossible; this patch inserts one instead of
aborting, and logs the state loss.

--- a/src/backend/renderer/gles/mod.rs
+++ b/src/backend/renderer/gles/mod.rs
@@ -2164,11 +2164,16 @@

 impl Renderer for GlesRenderer {
     fn context_id(&self) -> ContextId<GlesTexture> {
-        self.egl
-            .user_data()
-            .get::<ContextId<GlesTexture>>()
-            .unwrap()
-            .clone()
+        let user_data = self.egl.user_data();
+        match user_data.get::<ContextId<GlesTexture>>() {
+            Some(context_id) => context_id.clone(),
+            None => {
+                warn!("EGL renderer is missing its ContextId user data; inserting a new one");
+                user_data
+                    .get_or_insert_threadsafe(ContextId::<GlesTexture>::new)
+                    .clone()
+            }
+        }
     }

     fn downscale_filter(&mut self, filter: TextureFilter) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
